    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0260" n="1220" xml:id="pg1220"/>

                <head>No. 802.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bragg to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 24, 1888</date>.
                        (Received July 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 102.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed please find copy and translation
                    of a note to-day received from Mr. Mariscal, in reply to my request for the
                    arrest of Gulie Shields and Isaac Wilson, as made under your instruction No. 87,
                    of the 11th instant, notice of which request was conveyed in my No. 97, of
                    yesterday.</p>
                <p>This reply was not unexpected, but I did not call attention to the omission to
                    furnish any data from which an arrest could be made, in my No. 97, lest 1 might
                    seem to be disposed to be hypercritical.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwd. S. Bragg.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d89-a1.xml" xpointer="d89-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
